  <section id="why-it-matters" style="padding: 4rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb;">
    <div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.5rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 800; color: #111827; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Why Hoodie Manufacturing Matters More Than Ever in 2026</h2>
      <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1rem; max-width: 800px;">
        The hoodie is no longer just a casual garment. It is the anchor product for streetwear brands, athleisure lines, corporate merchandise programs, and university collections worldwide. The global streetwear market reached $371 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach $734 billion by 2034. Hoodies are the single most reordered product category in that market.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1rem; max-width: 800px;">
        But finding the right hoodie manufacturer is harder than it looks. Every factory can make a basic hoodie. Very few can consistently deliver heavyweight fleece with precise GSM tolerances, correct color matching across dye lots, and clean construction at the pockets, cuffs, and hood lining. These details are what separate a premium brand from a cheap one.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 1rem; max-width: 800px;">
        In 2026, EU regulations have added another layer of complexity. The EU ESPR now requires digital product passports for garments sold in Europe. Brands sourcing hoodies for the EU market must work with manufacturers that can provide full traceability from fiber to finished garment. Factories without this documentation put your entire EU distribution at risk.
      </p>
      <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; max-width: 800px;">
        This guide is built on 25 years of direct hoodie manufacturing experience. We have seen what works and what costs brands money. Here is everything you need to know.
      </p>
    </div>
