  <!-- HOODIE TYPES -->
  <section id="hoodie-types" style="padding: 4rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb; background: #f9fafb;">
    <div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.5rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 800; color: #111827; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Types of Hoodies and How They Affect Manufacturing</h2>
      <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: 700px;">
        Different hoodie styles have different production requirements, costs, and MOQs. Understanding this before you contact a factory saves time and prevents budget surprises.
      </p>
      <div style="display: grid; gap: 1.25rem;">
        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.75rem;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111827; margin: 0 0 0.6rem;">Pullover Hoodie</h3>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 0.6rem;">The simplest and most popular hoodie style. No zipper components required, which keeps production cost lower and MOQ more flexible. A pullover hoodie in 300 GSM cotton fleece can be produced from 100 pieces. This is the starting point for most new brands.</p>
          <p style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: #6b7280; margin: 0;"><strong>Extra cost vs plain sweatshirt:</strong> The kangaroo pocket, drawstring, and hood lining add approximately $1.20 to $2.50 per unit in extra labor and trim costs.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.75rem;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111827; margin: 0 0 0.6rem;">Zip-Up Hoodie (Full Zip)</h3>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 0.6rem;">Full-zip hoodies require a zipper, zipper tape, and zipper pull — all of which are sourced separately. This adds $1.50 to $4.00 per unit in component costs and can push MOQ up as zipper suppliers have their own minimum order requirements. YKK zippers are the industry standard and are worth specifying to avoid quality issues.</p>
          <p style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: #6b7280; margin: 0;"><strong>MOQ impact:</strong> Typically 150 to 300 pieces minimum for zip-up styles with custom branded zipper pulls.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.75rem;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111827; margin: 0 0 0.6rem;">Oversized Hoodie</h3>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 0.6rem;">Oversized hoodies require adjusted pattern grading and more fabric per unit, which increases material cost by 15 to 25 percent compared to regular fit styles. The most popular format for streetwear drops in 2026. Typically produced in 380 to 500 GSM for a premium look and feel.</p>
          <p style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: #6b7280; margin: 0;"><strong>Fabric cost impact:</strong> A 450 GSM oversized hoodie uses approximately 30% more fabric than a standard 300 GSM regular fit version.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.75rem;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111827; margin: 0 0 0.6rem;">Half-Zip Hoodie</h3>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 0.6rem;">A sportswear and athleisure staple. Half-zip hoodies require a shorter zipper and placket construction. Cost premium over a pullover is approximately $1.00 to $2.50 per unit. Popular for gym wear, running, and corporate branded merchandise.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.75rem;">
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111827; margin: 0 0 0.6rem;">Cropped Hoodie</h3>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 0.6rem;">Uses less fabric than a full-length hoodie but requires careful pattern work to maintain proportional hood and sleeve sizing. Popular in women's and unisex collections. Slightly lower material cost but same labor requirements as a standard pullover.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
