  <section id="certifications" style="padding: 4rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb; background: #f9fafb;">
    <div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.5rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 800; color: #111827; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Certifications and Compliance for Hoodie Manufacturing in 2026</h2>
      <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: 700px;">Selling hoodies in the USA, UK, EU, or Australia requires specific certifications. Here is what each one covers and how to verify it.</p>
      <div style="display: grid; gap: 1.25rem;">
        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: start;">
          <div style="background: #111827; color: #fff; font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 6px; text-align: center; white-space: nowrap;">OEKO-TEX</div>
          <div><h3 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111827; margin: 0 0 0.4rem;">OEKO-TEX Standard 100</h3><p style="color: #374151; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">Confirms the fleece fabric is free from harmful chemicals and substances. Critical for hoodies sold in EU markets and for any brand making health or safety claims. Verify at oeko-tex.com using the certificate number.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: start;">
          <div style="background: #111827; color: #fff; font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 6px; text-align: center; white-space: nowrap;">GOTS</div>
          <div><h3 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111827; margin: 0 0 0.4rem;">Global Organic Textile Standard</h3><p style="color: #374151; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">Required for any hoodie claiming to be made from organic cotton. Covers the entire supply chain from fiber to finished garment. Verify at global-standard.org.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: start;">
          <div style="background: #111827; color: #fff; font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 6px; text-align: center; white-space: nowrap;">BSCI</div>
          <div><h3 style="font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: #111827; margin: 0 0 0.4rem;">Business Social Compliance Initiative</h3><p style="color: #374151; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">Ethical labor audit standard required by most major EU retailers. Ask for the full audit report, not just the certificate. The report shows actual audit findings and any corrective actions taken.</p></div>
