  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section id="faq" style="padding: 4rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb; background: #f9fafb;">
    <div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.5rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 800; color: #111827; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div style="display: grid; gap: 1rem;">
        <details style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <summary style="font-weight: 700; color: #111827; cursor: pointer;">What is the minimum order quantity for hoodie manufacturers?</summary>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 1rem 0 0;">Most hoodie manufacturers require 100 to 300 pieces per style and color. Heavier customization like embroidery, custom zippers, and woven labels can push MOQ higher. Plain pullover hoodies tend to have lower MOQs than zip-up styles with branded hardware. SDF Clothing accepts orders from 100 pieces per style.</p>
        </details>
        <details style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <summary style="font-weight: 700; color: #111827; cursor: pointer;">How much does it cost to manufacture a hoodie in Bangladesh?</summary>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 1rem 0 0;">Hoodie manufacturing in Bangladesh costs between $8 and $28 per unit FOB depending on GSM, fabric type, and customization. Basic 280 GSM cotton fleece pullover hoodies start around $8 to $12. Premium 450 GSM heavyweight streetwear hoodies with screen printing and custom labels range from $18 to $28. Always calculate your total landed cost including freight and import duties before comparing quotes from different countries.</p>
        </details>
        <details style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <summary style="font-weight: 700; color: #111827; cursor: pointer;">What GSM is best for premium streetwear hoodies?</summary>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 1rem 0 0;">350 to 400 GSM is the sweet spot for premium streetwear hoodies. This weight gives a structured, substantial feel that justifies a higher retail price. Ultra-luxury or cold-climate brands often go up to 450 to 550 GSM. Standard retail hoodies use 280 to 320 GSM. Anything below 260 GSM is considered promotional weight and will feel thin to premium market buyers.</p>
        </details>
        <details style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <summary style="font-weight: 700; color: #111827; cursor: pointer;">How long does hoodie manufacturing take?</summary>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 1rem 0 0;">Standard hoodie production takes 30 to 60 days after sample approval. This covers fabric knitting or sourcing, dyeing, cutting, sewing, printing or embroidery, finishing, and quality inspection. Custom heavyweight hoodies with complex trims and embroidery can take 45 to 75 days. Always add 2 to 4 weeks for sample approval before counting your production lead time.</p>
        </details>
        <details style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <summary style="font-weight: 700; color: #111827; cursor: pointer;">Can I get private label hoodies with my own branding?</summary>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 1rem 0 0;">Yes. Full private label hoodie manufacturing includes custom woven neck labels, printed care labels, branded zipper pulls, custom drawstring aglets, hang tags, and branded poly bags. SDF Clothing provides complete private label production from 100 pieces. Always sign an NDA before sharing your brand assets or design files with any factory.</p>
        </details>
        <details style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <summary style="font-weight: 700; color: #111827; cursor: pointer;">What zipper should I specify for hoodie manufacturing?</summary>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 1rem 0 0;">Always specify YKK zippers by name in your tech pack. YKK is the global standard for quality zippers used by premium brands worldwide. Generic zippers can fail after a few wash cycles, creating returns and damaging brand trust. The cost premium for YKK over generic zippers is typically $0.80 to $2.50 per unit, which is well worth it to protect your brand reputation.</p>
        </details>
        <details style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <summary style="font-weight: 700; color: #111827; cursor: pointer;">Which country is best for manufacturing hoodies in 2026?</summary>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 1rem 0 0;">Bangladesh is the best overall choice for most brands in 2026. It offers competitive pricing, strong compliance infrastructure, BGMEA and BKMEA certified factories, and EU ESPR-ready documentation. China is better for very high volumes needing fast turnaround but faces tariff challenges for USA imports. Turkey is ideal for EU brands needing nearshore production with fast delivery times.</p>
        </details>
        <details style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <summary style="font-weight: 700; color: #111827; cursor: pointer;">Do hoodies shrink after washing and how do I prevent this?</summary>
          <p style="color: #374151; line-height: 1.75; margin: 1rem 0 0;">Cotton fleece hoodies can shrink 3 to 8 percent after the first wash if not pre-shrunk during production. Always request a pre-production shrinkage test report from your manufacturer. The factory should wash sample fabric, measure the shrinkage percentage, and adjust pattern pieces accordingly before cutting the bulk order. A good manufacturer will do this automatically. If they push back on shrinkage testing, that is a serious red flag.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

